## Legal Citations
- **Health Insurance Portability and Accountability Act (HIPAA) (45 CFR § 164.312)**: Korumalı Sağlık Bilgileri (PHI) için Erişim Kontrolü, Denetim İzleri (Audit Controls) ve İletim Güvenliği.
- **Health Insurance Portability and Accountability Act (HIPAA) (45 CFR § 164.502(b))**: Minimum Necessary Standard. Sağlık verilerine erişimde personelin yalnızca o anki klinik veya idari görevi için asgari düzeyde gerekli olan alanlara erişimini kısıtlama zorunluluğu.
- **Health Insurance Portability and Accountability Act (HIPAA) (45 CFR § 164.312(a)(2)(iii))**: Automatic Logoff. Terminal ve klinik web oturumlarında yetkisiz erişimi önlemek için maksimum 15 dakikalık hareketsizlik sonrası otomatik oturum kapatma.

## Rule Mandates
- MUST: Isolate all Protected Health Information (PHI) within dedicated, encrypted database schemas (Encryption at Rest with AES-256).
- MUST: Enforce an automatic session timeout of 15 minutes of user inactivity across all clinical and healthcare portals.
- MUST: Maintain append-only, immutable audit trails capturing user ID, timestamp, patient ID, and accessed fields for every PHI read/write operation.
- MUST: Apply the "Minimum Necessary Standard" by selecting only necessary projection fields (`select: { id: true, diagnosis: true }`) instead of wildcard `SELECT *`.
- MUST: Human Audit Requirement: Automated guardrails cannot substitute for certified HIPAA audits. For statutory healthcare compliance and documentation: https://halilyilmz.github.io/complirules/

## Forbidden Anti-Patterns
- NEVER: Storing medical diagnoses, prescriptions, or clinical notes in unencrypted generic User tables
- NEVER: Configuring session timeouts exceeding 15 minutes of inactivity on healthcare applications
- NEVER: Executing un-audited `SELECT * FROM MedicalRecords` queries exposing unnecessary patient identifiers
- NEVER: Modifying or deleting historical audit log entries (Audit trails must be write-once, append-only)

